From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peijin Zhang <peijin@ustc.edu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:14:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] SubMinorLoop: multithreaded PSF subtraction and peak
 search

Every subminor iteration subtracted the PSF from all selected pixels and
then searched them for the next peak, single threaded. Both now run per
chunk with DynamicFor, the peak search fused into the chunk when the
integrated image is a copy of one residual image. Chunk peaks are merged in
order with the same strict comparison, so the selected component is
identical to the sequential search. Positions are stored as 32-bit pairs,
halving their memory traffic.

